## Tips and common pitfalls

- **Photograph before you erase.** The parked ideas and the red-pen failure arrows on the boards belong in the draft too.
- **Split the transcription.** One person per template section gets it done in an evening.
- **Turn unsettled questions into open questions.** If the team didn't agree on something in the room, write it in §7 with an owner and a date rather than leaving it out.
- **Keep this version.** It is the baseline your revision is measured against.

